note The threads the window keeps busy and what the frame knows of each: a server per language with its batch and progress, the answers waiting for the next merge, and the link, rebuild, watcher and parent-map channels. working() is true while any of it is in flight. servers, no_server and indexing are keyed by server name, and a server in no_server failed to start and is never tried again. restart and relink record that the index changed while a batch or a link ran, so another one follows when it ends; last_merge is when answers last went into the index.

