file src/gui/mod.rs
symbol App
lines 0 47
hash 1d3946d0e37de3cc
note Everything the GUI knows, in one struct: the index and the map, the background work (Work), the server lookups (Lookup), the map on disk (MapFile), the reader's selection and History, the step views, the panel state, the fields and the graph. There is no model layer under it - a panel is a method that takes &mut self, draws, and queues Actions. Units and keys: now is seconds since the window opened; grids caches a drawn code block by (file, text hash, first line, last line); hscroll is each code block's horizontal offset in pixels; output_bottom counts frames left in which the log stays pinned to its end; base_why says why there is no base map. The selection: focus is the selected symbol, sel_path the path being read, sel_anchor its selected step when the selection came through the path, sel the listing's (anchor line, active line); scroll_to is a listing line to bring into view next frame, scroll_to_step a step to scroll to the document's top with the tries left, top_step the step whose header is topmost in the document, outline_shown the top step the outline last kept in view. steps holds the (path, step) views that differ from the default, dir_toggled the Files-tab directories whose default open state is flipped, groups_open the Paths-tab groups the reader opened or closed, peek the definition pinned in the right panel. tip_shown is the first line of last frame's tooltip, for dumps; results are (file, line) hits; shot is screenshot mode (write the window after a few frames, then quit) and shot_next a screenshot a script asked for on the next frame.

